    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d365-a2">

                <pb facs="0697" n="637" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg637"/>

                <head>General Schofield to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">War Department</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington City</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-07-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 2, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir.</hi> In connection with my letter of yesterday’s
                    date, inclosing copy of a telegram received from Brevet Major General Buchanan,
                    commanding the 5th military district, reporting the arrest of a party of
                    suspicious persons at Fort Livingston, I have the honor to send herewith a copy
                    of a communication received from the same officer, marked “confidential,” and
                    dated June 27, 1868, relative to an alleged Mexican expedition.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. M. SCHOFIELD, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of
                    War.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d365-a2-a1.xml" xpointer="d365-a2-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
